# DigitalOcean Third Blue-Green Slot — Datachain Rope (2026-05-03)

## Topology

The Datachain Rope mainnet (chainId 271828) now runs across **3 production nodes** in 2 cloud providers and 2 regions:

| Slot | Hostname | Provider | Region | IP | Disk | RAM | Role |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **BLUE (primary)** | `dcrope` | Gandi | Paris SD6 | `92.243.26.189` | 484 GB | 8 GB | active sequencer; Reth produces blocks |
| **GREEN (secondary)** | `dcrope-node2` | Gandi | Paris SD6 | `92.243.25.119` | — | 8 GB | hot-warm spare; receives state-sync from BLUE every 15 min |
| **DO (tertiary)** | `datachain-rpc-1` | DigitalOcean | Frankfurt (fra1) | `157.230.18.45` | 78 GB | 3.8 GB + 4 GB swap | hot-warm spare; receives state-sync from BLUE every 15 min (offset 7 min) |

All 3 nodes share **identical genesis hash** `0x6a425482c849cfa07ec253c272a661375469b71c47f499048218a377a24d7203` and `chainId 0x425d4 (271828)`.

## Public RPC failover order

Nginx upstream `digitalocean_rpc` (legacy name preserved for stability) on BLUE:

```nginx
upstream digitalocean_rpc {
    server host.docker.internal:8545 max_fails=2 fail_timeout=5s;  # BLUE primary
    server 92.243.25.119:8545 backup;                              # GREEN secondary
    server 157.230.18.45:8545 backup;                              # DO tertiary (added 2026-05-03)
}
```

Public traffic via `https://erpc.datachain.network` flows: **BLUE → GREEN if BLUE down → DO if both Gandi down**.

