## Cost / operational notes

- **No DigitalOcean LB** in front of DO droplets — saves ~$10/month. Failover is handled by Gandi nginx upstream.
- **Daily cost impact** of activating DO rpc-1 vs idle Python PoC: zero (droplet was already paid for and running).
- **Other 3 DO droplets** are still billed; if not needed as future witnesses or fourth slot, they can be destroyed for ~$120/year savings. **User decision pending.**

## Operational runbook

| Scenario | Action |
|---|---|
| BLUE Reth crashes | GREEN auto-takes traffic via nginx; bring BLUE back; sync resumes |
| BLUE + GREEN both down | DO auto-takes traffic via nginx (third backup); fix Gandi infra |
| DO mdbx corrupted | `ssh rope-vps 'sudo -u ubuntu /opt/datachain-rope/scripts/reth-do-bootstrap.sh'` (briefly stops BLUE, streams clean snapshot) |
| Promote a different DO droplet to fourth slot | Repeat the Reth+rope-node deployment on `167.172.106.174` (rpc-2, 78 GB), copy the cron sync, add to nginx upstream |
| Decommission DO entirely | Remove `server 157.230.18.45:8545 backup;` from nginx upstream, remove cron entry, `doctl droplet delete` (requires DO API token) |
